    "short_description": "The Algerian Ministry of National Education is the governmental body responsible for overseeing education in Algeria. Headquartered in El Mouradia, Algiers Province, it employs over 10,001 staff members. The ministry manages the national education system, which includes preparatory, primary, secondary, vocational, and higher education levels. Education is compulsory and free for children from ages 6 to 9.\n\nThe ministry's responsibilities encompass policy-making, administration, and implementation of educational programs. It focuses on foundational learning in primary education, builds on this in secondary education, and promotes vocational and technical training. The ministry also oversees higher education, emphasizing scientific research and development. It collaborates with international organizations, such as ALECSO, to enhance vocational education initiatives.",
